$ whycant -u www-data create /srv/inbox/upload.bin

✗ www-data (uid 33) cannot create /srv/inbox/upload.bin

  /                       drwxr-xr-x  root:root      ✓ traverse
  /srv                    drwxr-xr-x  root:root      ✓ traverse
  /srv/inbox              drwxrwx-w-  deploy:deploy  ✗ create in   ← blocked here
  /srv/inbox/upload.bin   ·           not evaluated

Why
  www-data is not the owner (deploy) and is not in group "deploy",
  so the "other" permissions apply: -w-. Creating an entry in a directory needs w and x.

Fixes (safest first)
  1. Grant write access to the directory only to www-data via ACL:
       sudo setfacl -m u:www-data:wx /srv/inbox
  2. Add www-data to the deploy group (restart the service afterwards):
       sudo usermod -aG deploy www-data
